    "guidance": "Observed reliability: 12/12 final-state successes (100%) from its own in-distribution replay entries; first success ranged from rollout step 282 to 575, making completion timing more variable than h02/h03. Every run had three gripper changes and zero unconverged IK steps. Use when blue is descending to or stable in blue_goal and red is observable, table-supported in the central buffer; the documented strongest case is after blue stabilizes and before red pickup, with red outside the 0.12 m horizontal red_goal switch radius and a conventional lift. Its phase-local anchors are designed for reachable translated red sources while switching to destination anchoring after lift, but source-translation generalization was not validated. Avoid an already-near-goal source, unusual low carry, slip, pose noise near anchor thresholds, changed nearest-object ordering, yaw-dominant variation, unstable blue, obstacles, or unreachable IK. Recognize failure through motion tied to blue/red/red_goal in the wrong phase, missed pickup, red remaining in the buffer, a low/slipping red causing the wrong switch, release outside full containment, more/oscillatory gripper changes versus the three seen in validation, blue displacement, or nonzero IK residuals/limit contacts. Terminal handoff: no successor; stop only when both goal predicates are observed, not on anchor identity, object height, closure, opening, or retreat alone."
  },
